WEBVTT

00:00:00.425 --> 00:00:07.742
You ask the agent to check your Gmail. It needs a key for that, so it asks for one. The request opens the vault on that name.

00:00:08.427 --> 00:00:13.654
You type the value into a hidden box, say what it is for, and which hosts it may be sent to.

00:00:14.328 --> 00:00:22.093
Save it. The vault lists the secret by name, purpose and hosts. The value is never shown again, not to you, and not to the model.

00:00:22.832 --> 00:00:29.104
You can edit a secret later, or remove it. Each person keeps their own, and the agent can have shared ones.
